  "notes": "No moving mountains, split earth or speaking dead drawn; 31:1-14 is not glossed (the tafsirs read the unstated answer differently). 31:34-46 is not glossed (Al-Muyassar names battles). Geometric for «بل لله الأمر جميعا», «لو يشاء الله لهدى الناس جميعا» and «إن الله لا يخلف الميعاد»; an hourglass for «فأمليت». 32:6-8 is not glossed (first person). STAGING v4: Both chapters stay ambient. c1 (31): a counterfactual (mountains moved, the earth split, the dead spoken to: never drawn), Allah's command and will, and the calamities on the disbelievers, which Al-Muyassar reads as battles: nothing staged; quiet over His command, His will and His promise (31:15-18, 31:24-29, 31:43-51). c2 (32): consolation to the Prophet ﷺ about the messengers mocked before him and Allah's respite and seizing (His first-person words): quiet over 32:6-13; hourglass kept."
 },
